# Sync invariants

- No scene-specific strings (no object/file names in solver or UI copy).
- Thresholds live in `core/sync/constants.py` (`ACCEPT_RMSE_PX`, `STRETCHED_PIXEL_RATIO`, `GROUND_PLANE_Z_FRACTION`, `GROUND_SLACK_DEFAULT`, `GROUND_Z_RESIDUAL_PX`, `LOG_SCALE_CLIP`, `BA_FREE_LANDMARK_LIMIT`, `SPATIAL_GRID_SIZE`, `SPATIAL_WEIGHT_CLIP`, `RADIAL_WEIGHT_GAIN`, `TRIANGULATION_GN_STEPS`, `TRIANGULATION_ANGLE_WEIGHT_FLOOR`, `TRIANGULATION_PARALLEL_COSINE`, `MIRROR_SLACK_DEFAULT`, `MIRROR_PLANE_RESIDUAL_PX`, `MIRROR_PAIR_HARD_GAP`, `MIRROR_PAIR_RESIDUAL_PX`, `SYNC_WEIGHT_PROTECT`). Do not add a second peel/accept cutoff.
- Copying locked K onto another still: exact portrait/landscape swap (e.g. 3000×4000 ↔ 4000×3000) swaps fx/fy and cx/cy. Any other size change: fx and fy share one scale (square pixels). Solve Sync may set fy=fx when they already differ by more than `STRETCHED_PIXEL_RATIO`.
- Solve order: register (strongest-pair seed, then easiest-next camera) → peel above `ACCEPT_RMSE_PX` → BA (pose-only above the free-landmark limit, then thaw 3D if it helps) → peel → resect skipped (full cloud, then ground tags) → triangulate landmarks now visible in recovered views and PnP stills that had no cloud support. A recovered camera must not fail the joint RMSE.
- If you add/move a stage or module, update the map in `AGENTS.md` in the same change.
- Docstrings: short contracts on entry/stage functions only, not changelogs.
- User-facing changelog lines stay non-solver-jargon (see `CHANGELOG.md`).
